    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11167" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cordŭēna</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γορδυηνή</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a district of Greater
				Armenia</i>, now <i>Kurdistan</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 8, 20
			al.</span></i>—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cordŭēni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Corduena</i>, now <i>the
			Kurds</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. H. 4, 60</span></i> Dietsch; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 15,
				17, § 44</span></i>; Sext. <i><span class="en">Ruf.
				Brev. 20</span></i>.—Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gordyaei</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i><span class="en">Curt. 5, 1,
				14</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 4, 10, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 11,
				12, § 30</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
